# Vercel's CLI uploads the working directory, and `backend/.env` is read by
# backend/config.py's SettingsConfigDict(env_file=...). Without this, a local
# dev .env ships to production and supplies every value the platform does not
# override - which is how a preview deployment came up announcing
# `http://localhost:3000` as an allowed CORS origin.
.env
.env.*
*.env
backend/.env
backend/.env.*

# Not needed at runtime, and they are most of the bundle.
#
# `frontend` must NOT go here. Vercel applies this file to every project in
# the repository, including the frontend's own Git deployments - it logs
# "Found .vercelignore (repository root)" and strips the matches before the
# build runs. Listing it here deleted the frontend's source out of its own
# build, which then failed with "Couldn't find any pages or app directory".
# The backend keeps it out of the function bundle through excludeFiles in
# vercel.json instead, which is scoped to the backend's own function.
.git
.github
docs
backend/tests
# backend/alembic is deliberately NOT excluded: #36 runs migrations as a
# deploy step, and .vercelignore drops files from the upload entirely, so
# excluding them would leave the build with nothing to migrate from.
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/node_modules
.vercel/output

# Local tooling and leftovers.
.claude
.vscode
.logs
*.deb
Makefile
